### Order To Cash — service liveness
###
### Every backend service is a HYBRID app: it listens on HTTP *and* on NATS
### and/or Kafka. Only the HTTP side is reachable from this file — the
### business operations (orders.create, fulfillment.stock.reserve,
### billing.credit.hold, ...) are NATS request-reply. They are reachable over
### HTTP through the Gateway, which landed in feature 25 — see gateway.http.
###
### Start a service with, e.g.:  pnpm dev:orders
### Ports come from .env (defaults below match .env.example).

@gateway       = http://localhost:3001
@orders        = http://localhost:3002
@fulfillment   = http://localhost:3003
@billing       = http://localhost:3004
@notifications = http://localhost:3005
@projector     = http://localhost:3006

### Orders — the aggregate, the outbox relay and the saga orchestrator live here
GET {{orders}}/

### Fulfillment — stock reservations and despatch advice
GET {{fulfillment}}/

### Billing — buyer credit, and (from feature 21) invoicing
GET {{billing}}/

### Gateway — REST/OpenAPI + SSE (feature 25). The real requests are in gateway.http.
GET {{gateway}}/

### Notifications — SMTP (Mailpit) / console notification port (feature 23).
GET {{notifications}}/

### Projector — Kafka facts -> MongoDB order_timeline (feature 24).
GET {{projector}}/

### A healthy reply looks like:  { "service": "orders", "status": "ok" }
### Real readiness probes (DB / Kafka / NATS indicators via @nestjs/terminus)
### arrive with feature 27; this endpoint proves the process is up, no more.
